    {
      "id": "story-frame-5",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1050,
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "name": "Slide 05",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#202020",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "locked": false,
      "seed": 105,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1148738892,
      "customData": {
        "title": "What research taught me",
        "spoken": "I used research to help make three choices. First, the FaceNet paper showed how a computer can turn a face into numbers that can be compared. That supported my idea of checking one person against one ticket. Second, I found research showing that those numbers can still reveal private information. So I changed them for each event, rather than using one reusable version everywhere. But I cannot claim this makes them impossible to recover. Third, I learned about digital signatures, which are like a stamp that helps the gate check that a ticket is genuine. These papers helped with the design; they are not test results for my app.",
        "keyPoints": "1. Research explained how to compare faces.\n2. Face data still has privacy risks.\n3. Signatures help check a ticket is genuine; papers are not my results.",
        "originalSlideText": "RESEARCH\nThree sources that shaped my design.\nPublished results guided decisions; they were not Private Pass test results.\nPrivate Pass  /  MANAV CODATY\n05\nSchroff et al. (2015)\nFaces can be compared as numerical data.\nUse a trained model for a 1:1 check.\nMai et al. (2019) + Rathgeb & Uhl (2011)\nA face template can still reveal information.\nUse event-specific data. Avoid claiming anonymity.\nJosefsson & Liusvaara (2017)\nSignatures show if a pass was changed.\nLet the gate check passes offline.",
        "sources": [
          "/Users/manavcodaty/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Praco Family/EPQ/Mav/PrivatePass_EPQ Presentation_v4.pptx — slide 5"
        ],
        "claim": "What research taught me"
      },
      "index": "au",
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793174454816,
      "link": null
    },
