    {
      "id": "story-frame-12",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 5400,
      "y": 2100,
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "name": "Slide 12",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#202020",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "locked": false,
      "seed": 112,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 996265204,
      "customData": {
        "title": "Detailed test evidence",
        "spoken": "This slide is the most important evidence from my testing. The saved records from 15 June show checks of ticket claims, who is allowed to claim them, ticket limits, safe retries, signed passes, stopping a reused ticket, and sending entry records back later. I also checked local networking and launched both phone apps on a real iPhone. During development, I found and fixed problems with face cropping, repeat ticket requests and saving used tickets. But these records are mainly software tests. They do not show a complete physical test of every step on the final version. I later saw the whole journey work, but I did not keep a detailed record from that run. I also didn't collect enough attempts to measure face accuracy or test whether photos or screens could fool it. So I can show which parts worked, but I can't claim the system is ready for a real event.",
        "keyPoints": "1. 15 June records: ticket, retry, replay, sync and networking checks.\n2. Bugs found and fixed during development.\n3. Full later run observed, not fully documented.\n4. No measured face accuracy, fake-face or real-event results.",
        "originalSlideText": "TESTING  /  EVIDENCE REVIEW\nWhat testing proved — and what it didn’t\nRECORDED CHECKS\n✓\nTICKETS & RULES\nBrowser/automated: ticket claims, ownership, capacity and access.\n✓\nRETRIES\nIdempotent claim requests handled without unwanted duplicates.\n✓\nSIGNING & REPLAY\nPass authenticity and reused-ticket rejection covered by tests.\n✓\nSYNC & REVOCATION\nSigned sync and cancellation refresh logic checked in software.\n✓\nIPHONE + LOCAL WI-FI\nApps installed/launched; iPhone communicated with the Mac locally.\nWHAT BROKE → WHAT I FIXED\nCROPPING\nUneven face crops → shared crop rules.\nCLAIM RETRIES\nLost response → persistent request ID.\nREPLAY SAFETY\nSave used-ticket state before “accepted”.\nNOT PROVEN / NOT TESTED ENOUGH\n—\nFULL PHONE JOURNEY\nLater observed, but no detailed dated final receipt.\n—\nFACE ACCURACY\nNo genuine/impostor trials or FAR / FRR figures.\n—\nSPOOF RESISTANCE\nNo retained structured photo, screen or mask trials.\n—\nREAL-WORLD USE\nNo repeated queue timings, user study or field rollout.\nPrivate Pass  /  MANAV CODATY\n12A",
        "sources": [
          "/Users/manavcodaty/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Praco Family/EPQ/Mav/PrivatePass_EPQ Presentation_v4.pptx — slide 12"
        ],
        "claim": "Detailed test evidence"
      },
      "index": "b1d",
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793174454816,
      "link": null
    },
