      "seed": 113,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 238429772,
      "customData": {
        "title": "The short evidence summary",
        "spoken": "So the short version is this: I have saved results for important software checks. I also saw the full system work later, but didn't keep enough detail to prove that whole run in the same way. And I didn't properly measure face accuracy, fake-face attacks or how fast it would be with lots of people. That difference between what I saw and what I can prove matters to my final answer.",
        "keyPoints": "1. Some software tests are recorded.\n2. Whole journey was later observed, but not fully documented.\n3. Face performance and real-world use are still unknown.",
        "originalSlideText": "TESTING\nWhat the evidence really shows.\nI separated saved tests, my own observation, and what I never measured.\nPrivate Pass  /  MANAV CODATY\n12\nRECORDED\nAutomated, browser, simulator and local-network checks. Apps launched on a real iPhone.\nLATER OBSERVED\nI saw the full journey work, but did not keep a detailed final test record.\nNOT MEASURED\nFace accuracy, spoof resistance, queue speed, user experience and public rollout.",
        "sources": [
          "/Users/manavcodaty/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Praco Family/EPQ/Mav/PrivatePass_EPQ Presentation_v4.pptx — slide 13"
        ],
        "claim": "The short evidence summary"
      },
      "index": "b1m",
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
