    {
      "id": "story-frame-16",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 5400,
      "y": 3150,
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "name": "Slide 16",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#202020",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "locked": false,
      "seed": 116,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1677334260,
      "customData": {
        "title": "What could go wrong?",
        "spoken": "Before using this at a real event, I would need to deal with three things. First, an offline gate may still accept a ticket that was cancelled after it lost internet. Second, simply seeing a face in the camera doesn't mean it's a real person. A photo or screen might be a problem, and I didn't complete proper tests for that. Third, I would need to know whether people can use it easily, including anyone who doesn't want a face check. I'd test all three before calling it safe for a real crowd.",
        "keyPoints": "1. Offline cancellations can be out of date.\n2. Face presence is not proof against photos.\n3. Need usability and non-face alternatives.",
        "originalSlideText": "LIMITATIONS\nWhat could go wrong at a real event?\nPrivate Pass  /  MANAV CODATY\n15\nCANCELLED TICKETS\nOffline gates have an old cancellation list.\nUse shorter validity and refresh rules.\nFAKE FACES\nFace detected does not mean real person.\nRun photo, screen and mask tests.\nUSABILITY\nThere was no retained user or fallback study.\nTest accessibility and manual entry.",
        "sources": [
          "/Users/manavcodaty/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Praco Family/EPQ/Mav/PrivatePass_EPQ Presentation_v4.pptx — slide 16"
        ],
        "claim": "What could go wrong?"
      },
      "index": "b2X",
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793174454816,
      "link": null
    },
