    {
      "id": "story-frame-18",
      "type": "frame",
      "x": 1800,
      "y": 4200,
      "width": 1600,
      "height": 900,
      "name": "Slide 18",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#202020",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "locked": false,
      "seed": 118,
      "version": 2,
      "versionNonce": 1443614028,
      "customData": {
        "title": "Final answer",
        "spoken": "So, did Private Pass answer my question? My answer is yes, but only for a small, prepared prototype. I built the four parts of the ticket journey, and I have evidence for important checks like ticket rules and stopping reuse. I also saw the whole process work together. But I didn't keep a complete record of that later run, and I haven't proved how well the face check would work at a crowded event. For me, the project showed that the idea is possible, and also how much testing is needed before it can be trusted.",
        "keyPoints": "1. Yes, for a prepared prototype.\n2. Key software checks worked; whole journey later observed.\n3. More testing needed before a real event.",
        "originalSlideText": "FINAL ANSWER\nA working prototype — not a finished product.\nPrivate Pass shows this approach is possible in a prepared setup.\nPrivate Pass  /  MANAV CODATY\n17\nWHAT I CAN SHOW\nThe ticket, face check and offline gate can work together.\nWHAT I CANNOT CLAIM\nAccuracy at scale, strong anti-spoofing or readiness for public events.\nREAL TESTS ARE STILL NEEDED BEFORE LIVE DEPLOYMENT",
        "sources": [
          "/Users/manavcodaty/Library/Mobile Documents/com~apple~CloudDocs/Praco Family/EPQ/Mav/PrivatePass_EPQ Presentation_v4.pptx — slide 18"
        ],
        "claim": "Final answer"
      },
      "index": "b30",
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793174454816,
      "link": null
    },
